<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon.png">
<link rel="shortcut icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any">
<meta name="application-name" content="The Axiom">
<title>Morse code · The Axiom</title>
<style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#edf3ef;color:#18362d;font:16px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:900px;margin:auto;padding:20px 16px}a{color:#176b4d}section{background:#fff;border:1px solid #cfdfd6;border-radius:12px;padding:16px;margin:16px 0}h1,h2{line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:0}label{display:block;font-weight:650}textarea{width:100%;resize:vertical;min-height:100px;font:inherit;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aac5b7;border-radius:8px}button{font:inherit;font-weight:650;color:white;background:#176b4d;border:0;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;min-height:44px;cursor:pointer}button:disabled{opacity:.55;cursor:default}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,textarea:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #c38d32;outline-offset:3px}.actions,.settings{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin:8px 0}.settings label{flex:1;min-width:130px}.settings input{width:100%;font:inherit;padding:8px;border:1px solid #aac5b7;border-radius:8px}.reference{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(108px,1fr));gap:6px}.reference div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:6px;background:#edf3ef;padding:6px 8px;border-radius:5px}.reference code{font-size:1rem;white-space:nowrap}.muted{color:#536e61}
</style><script src="/api/tools/morse.js" defer></script></head>
<body><main><a href="/">← Back to library</a><h1>Morse code</h1>
<p>International Morse code reference and translator. All processing happens on this device, without internet access or downloads.</p>
<noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to use the translator and microphone decoder.</p></noscript>
<section aria-labelledby="translate-title"><h2 id="translate-title">Text and Morse translator</h2>
<p>Separate Morse characters with spaces and words with a slash or three spaces. Unsupported characters are marked rather than silently removed.</p>
<label for="morse-input">Input</label><textarea id="morse-input" placeholder="SOS or ... --- ..." spellcheck="false" maxlength="20000"></textarea>
<div class="actions"><button id="morse-encode" type="button">Encode text</button><button id="morse-decode" type="button">Decode Morse</button></div>
<label for="morse-output">Result</label><textarea id="morse-output" readonly></textarea><button id="morse-use-output" type="button">Use result as input</button><p id="morse-notice" role="status"></p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="mic-title"><h2 id="mic-title">Microphone decoder (experimental)</h2>
<p>Play a clean Morse tone through speakers or use a microphone connected to your radio. Automatic detection estimates pitch and speed from the first several tones; background noise, uneven spacing, weak signals and browser timing can cause errors. This is not a dependable emergency communications decoder.</p>
<p>Microphone access requires a trusted HTTPS connection (or browser-supported localhost) and permission. Audio is processed only in memory on this device; it is not recorded, saved or transmitted. Listening stops when you leave or hide this page.</p>
<label><input id="mic-auto" type="checkbox" checked> Automatically detect pitch and speed</label>
<div class="settings"><label for="mic-speed">Speed (WPM)<input id="mic-speed" type="number" min="5" max="30" value="15" required></label>
<label for="mic-frequency">Pitch (Hz)<input id="mic-frequency" type="number" min="400" max="1200" step="10" value="700" required></label>
<label for="mic-threshold">Threshold (dB)<input id="mic-threshold" type="number" min="-90" max="-20" value="-75" required></label></div>
<p class="muted">Automatic mode is recommended. If the meter moves but no tones are detected, lower the threshold; if background noise causes false marks, raise it. Keep this page visible while listening.</p>
<div class="actions"><button id="mic-start" type="button">Start microphone</button><button id="mic-stop" type="button" disabled>Stop microphone</button></div>
<p id="mic-status" role="status">Microphone is off.</p>
<label for="mic-level">Microphone input level</label><meter id="mic-level" min="0" max="100" value="0" style="width:100%;height:22px"></meter>
<p id="mic-metrics" class="muted">Start listening to see the input level, detected pitch, speed and tone activity.</p><p>Current Morse symbols: <code id="mic-symbols">—</code></p>
<label for="mic-output">Decoded audio</label><textarea id="mic-output" readonly></textarea></section>
<section aria-labelledby="reference-title"><h2 id="reference-title">International Morse reference</h2>
<p>A dash is three dot units. Gaps are one unit within a character, three between characters, and seven between words. SOS is conventionally sent as a continuous prosign <code>...---...</code>; ordinary S O S text encodes as <code>... --- ...</code>.</p>
<div id="morse-reference" class="reference"></div>
<p class="muted">Alphabet, digits and common punctuation; does not cover every national extension or procedural signal. Timing follows International Morse (ITU-R M.1677-1).</p></section>
</main></body></html>
